<title>NORWAY: Ekofisk oil output back to normal - Phillips.</title>
<headline>Ekofisk oil output back to normal - Phillips.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Phillips Petroleum said on Wednesday that crude production at the North Sea Ekofisk oilfield was back to normal at 350,000 barrels per day following its restart on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We're back to full production. That happened about three hours after we started up yesterday,&quot; a spokesman for Phillips said.</p>
<p>The development resumed output at 1240 GMT on Tuesday following a one week unscheduled shutdown due to a gas leak in an oil pipeline.</p>
<p>Output from third party fields -- British Petroleum's Gyda and Ula and Amoco's Valhall and Hod -- and the Statpipe gas line was uninterrupted by the shutdown.</p>
<p>-- Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
